{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310745,"nonce":"MJ+EutcL5I3+ZMmN9TNqEDYupoE=","title":"Stdlib cache creates bare-name function stubs that cause WASM import collisions and non-deterministic forwarder resolution","message":"The MIR's Phase 1 registration creates bare-name function stubs (\"get\", \"set\", \"alloc\") for extern\nclass methods. These stubs are dead code — the MIR's CallDirect uses qualified function IDs\n(\"haxe_bytes_get\") from the stdlib mapping in Phase 2. But the bare stubs persist in the module\n(via blade cache) and create collision-prone WASM imports.\n\n**Why stubs can't be removed:** The WASM backend uses sequential index assignment. Removing any\nfunction shifts ALL subsequent indices, breaking CallDirect targets for other functions.\n\n**Why stubs can't be renamed:** The qualified name already exists in the module (from Phase 2),\ncausing name collisions.\n\n\nMIR dump shows BOTH entries for the same logical method:\n- `IrFunctionId(17) name=\"haxe_bytes_get\" blocks=0 in_extern=true kind=ExternC` — qualified (used by CallDirect)\n- `IrFunctionId(170555) name=\"get\" blocks=0 in_extern=false kind=ExternC` — bare (dead code)\n\n\nJS harness provides bare-name aliases that route to qualified handle-table implementations:\n`get: (...a) =\u003e rayzor.haxe_bytes_get(...a)`\n\n\nFix at the source — prevent bare stubs from being created:\n1. **Option A**: In `hir_to_mir.rs` Phase 1, skip `register_function_signature` for extern class\n   methods. Requires detecting extern classes during stdlib compilation (is_extern flag).\n2. **Option B**: In the blade cache serialization, filter out bare-name stubs before caching.\n3. **Option C**: Change WASM backend to use stable index assignment (hash-based, not sequential)\n   so function removal doesn't shift indices.\n\n**Key files:** `compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs` (Phase 1 at line 2253), `src/main.rs` (JS aliases),\n`compiler/src/codegen/wasm_backend.rs` (collect_imports sequential indexing)\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_wasm_bare_stubs` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}